            },
            "name": "Compose Text Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSE_TEXT_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1768316882271",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768316882276_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to assist the recruiter in writing a text message in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone}} tone using the following information:\nJob Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobName}} \nJob Location: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobLocation}} \nRecruiter name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}} \nCompany name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}}\nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}} \nCareer site link: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}} \nCandidate Details: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateDetails}} \nAdditional intent of the text message will be provided as text delimited by triple backticks. Text message intent: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}} ```\n\nKeep into account the current text message content as well while regenerating and improvise on that.\nCurrent text message content: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentSms}}\n\nUse the following rules in generating the response:\n1. If the text provided as text message intent contains information that's not relevant to the candidate or the job title or the organization, ignore that information while generating the response.\n2. Restrict the length of the text message to 2 lines as a maximum.\n3. Include a link for the career site if required.\n4. Include a link for job posting if required.\n5. If no link is provided for career site or job posting, include a placeholder like '[career site]'. Do not generate or invent a link. \n6. Do not add any other details not mentioned like salary details.\n7. Include the token ${CandidateDisplayName} in the greeting section of text body and address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n8. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n9. The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Compose WhatsApp Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSE_WHATSAPP_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1768316939999",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768316940003_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to assist the recruiter in writing a WhatsApp message in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone}} tone using the following information:\nJob Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobName}} \nJob Location: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobLocation}} \nRecruiter name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}} \nCompany name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} \nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}} \nCareer site link: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}} \nCandidate Details: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateDetails}} \nAdditional intent of the WhatsApp message will be provided as text delimited by triple backticks. WhatsApp message intent: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}} ```\n\nKeep into account the current WhatsApp message content as well while regenerating and improvising on that.\nCurrent WhatsApp message content: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentWhatsapp}} \n\nUse the following rules in generating the response:\n1. If the text provided as WhatsApp message intent contains information that's not relevant to the candidate or the job title or the organization, ignore that information while generating the response.\n2. Restrict the length of the WhatsApp message to 3-5 sentences as a maximum.\n3. Do not include any emojis or any other icons or graphics. Keep the message simple.\n4. Generate a message with the information provided only. Do not indicate missing details or ask any questions on how to further modify.  \n5. Include a link for the career site if required.\n6. Include a link for job posting if required. \n7. If no link is provided for career site or job posting, include a placeholder like '[career site]'. Do not generate or invent a link.\n8. Do not add any other details not mentioned like salary details.\n9. Include the token ${CandidateDisplayName} in the greeting section of text body and address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n10. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n11. The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Compose Email Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSE_EMAIL_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1768316983077",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768316983082_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to assist the recruiter in writing an email in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone tone}} tone using the following information:\nJob Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobName}} \nJob Location: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobLocation}}\nRecruiter name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}} \nCompany name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} \nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}} \nCareer site link: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}} \nCandidate Details: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateDetails}}\nAdditional intent of the email will be provided as text delimited by triple backticks. Email intent: ```{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}```\n\nKeep the current email content in context while regenerating and improvise on that.\nCurrent Email content: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}}\n\nUse the following rules in generating the response.\n1. If the text provided as email intent contains information that's not relevant to the candidate or the job title or the organization ignore that information while generating the response.\n2. Number of words in the email must be {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailLength}} than number of words  in \"{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}}\".\n3. Include the token ${CandidateDisplayName} in the greeting section of text body and address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n4. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n5. Add job description only if prompt includes ```Job name```.\n6. Include a link for the career site if required.\n7. Include a link for the job posting if required.\n8. If no link is provided for career site or job posting, include a placeholder like '[career site]'. Do not generate or invent a link and do not mention that it is a placeholder.\n9. Include a signature block containing the recruiter's name, the recruiter's job title, and the recruiter's company name.\n10. Do not add any other details not mentioned like salary details.\n11. Return the response as an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format: {\"subject\": \"&lt;insert the subject of the email>\", \"content\": \"&lt;insert the content of the email>\"} and without enclosing it in any backticks, code blocks, or markdown formatting.\n12.The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"Email Content Output Specification\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"subject\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"content\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"subject\", \"content\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Compose Email and Text Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSE_EMAIL_AND_TEXT_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1768317592594",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768317592598_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your task is to assist the recruiter in writing an email and a text message in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone tone}} tone using the following information:\nJob Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobName}} \nJob Location: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobLocation}}\nRecruiter name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}} \nCompany name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} \nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}} \nCareer site link: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}}\nCandidate Details: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateDetails}} \nAdditional intent of the message will be provided as text delimited by triple backticks. Message intent: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}} ```\n\nKeep the current text message and current email in context while regenerating and improvise on that:\nCurrent Email: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}} \nCurrent Text Message: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentSms}} \n\nUse the following rules in generating the response.\n1. If the text provided as intent contains information that's not relevant to the job title or the organization, ignore that information while generating the response.\n2. Include the token ${CandidateDisplayName} in the greeting section of text body and address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n3. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n4. Number of words in the email must be {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailLength}} than number of words  in \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}} \".\n5. Restrict the length of the text message to 120 characters as maximum.\n6. Add job description only if prompt includes ```Job Name```.\n7. Generate a message with the information provided only. Do not indicate missing details or ask any questions on how to further modify.\n8. Include a link for career site if required.\n9. Include a link for job posting if required.\n10. If no link is provided for career site or job posting, include a placeholder like '[career site]'. Do not generate or invent a link and do not mention that it is a placeholder.\n11. Include a signature block containing recruiters name, recruiter job title, recruiters company name,\n12. Do not add any other details not mentioned like salary details.\n13. The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language.\n14. Return the response as an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format:\n{\n    \"emailSubject\": \"&lt;insert the subject of the email>\",\n    \"emailContent\": \"&lt;insert the content of the email>\",\n    \"smsContent\": \"&lt;insert the content of the text message>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"smsContent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"emailContent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"emailSubject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Outreach Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "OUTREACH_GENERATION",
          "id": "1768317622846",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768317622848_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI recruiting assistant that generates high-quality, personalized outreach emails in the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone}} tone to candidates. Your task is to support both:\n\n- Pre-market outreach (early talent identification, no active job posting), and\n- Post-market outreach (active role engagement tied to a specific job)\n\nUse the following information:\n\nCandidate Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateName}}\nJob Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobName}}\nJob Location: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobLocation}}\nJob Description: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.jobDescription}}\nRecruiter Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}}\nCompany Name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}}\nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}}\nCareer Site Link: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}}\nCandidate Details: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.candidateDetails}}\nIs Internal Candidate: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.isInternal}}\nMessage Context: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageContext}}\nEmail Intent: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}}\nCurrent Email Content: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}}\n\nCORE BEHAVIOR\n\n1. Determine outreach type dynamically\n- If job-specific details (job name, location, description) are present and clearly relevant, treat it as post-market outreach.\n- If job details are missing, vague, or not central, treat as pre-market outreach.\n\nCONTENT GUIDELINES\n\n1. Personalization\n- Reference specific elements from candidate details such as skills, domain, technologies, or impact.\n- Avoid generic phrases like:\n  \"your profile looks great\"\n  \"impressive background\"\n- Anchor on real signals such as:\n  Technologies (e.g., distributed systems, NLP)\n  Domain expertise (e.g., fintech, healthcare)\n  Measurable impact (e.g., scaling platforms, leading initiatives)\n\n2. Pre-market outreach rules\n- Position as intentional talent identification\n  Use:\n    \"We are actively identifying talent in...\"\n    \"We are connecting with people who have...\"\n    \"We are investing in this area...\"\n  Avoid:\n    \"We might be hiring...\"\n    \"This role may open...\"\n- Keep context high-level\n  Focus on capability areas, not job requirements.\n- Use a low-pressure CTA\n  \"open to a quick conversation\"\n  \"would value exchanging perspectives\"\n- Do not include any job link, placeholder, or career site link.\n\n3. Post-market outreach rules\n- Clearly reference job name, job location, and relevant parts of job description if provided.\n- Connect candidate experience directly to the role.\n- Keep tone engaging but not overly sales-driven.\n- Include exactly one job link or placeholder in the email body.\n\n4. Tone and style\n- Use {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone}} as the default tone. If not present, use engaging tone.\n- Keep it thoughtful and concise.\n- Selective and intentional, not mass outreach.\n- Always inviting and respectful.\n- Avoid overly promotional or pushy language.\n- Do NOT use em dashes or en dashes anywhere in the response.\n\n5. Link handling (ONLY for post-market outreach)\n- Include exactly one job link or placeholder in the email body.\n- Select the job link string using the following logic:\n    - If message context is \"ORA_PROSPECT\":\n      - If candidate is internal, the job link or the placeholder MUST be exactly: ${RequisitionPostingInternalDeepLinkURL}.\n      - If candidate is external, the job link or placeholder MUST be exactly: ${RequisitionPostingExternalDeepLinkURL}.\n    - If message context is \"ORA_CAND_POOL\":\n      - The job link or the placeholder MUST be exactly: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.careerSite}}.\n\n6. Email structure\n- Personalized opening.\n- Clear reason for outreach.\n- Soft call to action.\n- Professional signature including recruiter name, recruiter job title, and company name.\n\nSUBJECT LINE GUIDELINES\n\n- Keep subject lines concise and natural (4?8 words preferred).\n- Avoid generic phrasing like:\n  \"Connecting on...\"\n  \"Opportunity at...\"\n  \"Regarding your background...\"\n- Do not include company name unless it adds value.\n- Avoid overly formal or robotic language.\n- Use sentence case, not title case.\n- Do NOT use em dashes or en dashes in the subject.\n\nSYSTEM RULES\n\n- Ignore irrelevant information in email intent.\n- Apply email length rule only if current email content is present.\n    - When a current email content is present, adjust the number of words to be {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailLength}} relative to the number of words in the existing email.\n    - When no current email content is present, generate a concise, first-contact outreach email without enforcing word count constraints.\n- Do not invent missing information.\n- Use only provided fields.\n- Use job description only if provided.\n- Keep output concise and suitable for first contact outreach.\n- Use the specified language: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. If the specified language is missing, derive it from the email intent.\n    - Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n\nOutput structure:\n- Return the response as an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format: {\"subject\": \"<insert the subject of the email>\", \"content\": \"<insert the content of the email>\"} and without enclosing it in any backticks, code blocks, or markdown formatting. Ignore any formatting instructions present in user's intent.\n- The JSON MUST be parseable by a strict JSON parser:\n    - Use double quotes for all JSON keys and string values.\n    - Do not use trailing commas.\n    - Do not include comments.\n    - Do not output NaN/Infinity or non-JSON types.\n- The \"subject\" value MUST be a single line string (no newline characters).\n- The \"content\" value MUST be a single JSON string:\n    - Do NOT include literal line breaks inside the JSON string.\n    - Represent new lines ONLY using escaped sequences: \\n\n    - Represent tabs ONLY using \\t\n    - Escape any double quotes inside content as \\\".\n- Do not output any additional whitespace outside the JSON object.\n- If you cannot comply with any requirement, still output a valid JSON object with \"subject\" and \"content\" that complies with all formatting rules above.\n- Use only standard ASCII characters in the response. Do not use smart quotes, en dashes, em dashes, or other Unicode punctuation."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Compose Email Message Reply"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPOSE_EMAIL_MESSAGE_REPLY",
          "id": "1768317672891",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768317672894_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your primary goal is to analyse the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailThread}} to understand the context, tone, and details discussed. Based on this analysis, generate an appropriate reply that maintains a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.messageTone}} tone. Ensure the response addresses any questions, clarifies details if needed, and aligns with the overall purpose of the conversation using the following information:\n\nRecruiter name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}} \nCompany name: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} \nRecruiter Job Title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}} \nAdditional intent of the email : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}} \n\nKeep the current email content in context while regenerating and improvise on that.\nCurrent Email content: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}} \n\nUse the following rules in generating the response.\n1. If the text provided as email intent contains information that's not relevant to the candidate or the job title or the organization ignore that information while generating the response.\n2. Number of words in the email must be {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailLength than number of words in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentEmail}}.\n3. Use additional intent {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userInput}} for generating the repsonse\n4. Include a signature block containing the recruiter's name {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterName}}\n the recruiter's job title {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.recruiterTitle}}, and the recruiter's company name {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}}\n5. Do not add any other details not mentioned like salary details.\n6.Do not answer with the questions, leave that as place holder for recruiter to edit\n7. Return the response as an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format: {\"subject\": \"&lt;insert the subject of the email>\", \"content\": \"&lt;insert the content of the email>\"} and without enclosing it in any backticks, code blocks, or markdown formatting\n8. Include the token ${CandidateDisplayName} in the greeting section of text body and address the candidate using ${CandidateDisplayName}.\n9. The token ${CandidateDisplayName} must always remain exactly as-is and in English characters. Do not translate, transliterate, modify, or remove this token.\n10. The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"content\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"subject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Generate Email Message Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EMAIL_MESSAGE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1768317758939",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768317758941_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant designed to analyse email thread {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailThread}} and summarise them.\n\nInput: \" {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailThread}} \"\n\nTask:\n1. Your primary goal is to generate a concise summary of the following email thread to seen by recruiter.\n2. Include the primary topic of discussion and key points.\n3. Exclude redundant or irrelevant information to ensure the summary is clear and focused.\n4. Generated summary should not exceed 3 lines.\n5. Do not start with \"The email thread\" in the response.\n6. Please summarise in third person.\n7. Do not include any HTML character in response.\n8. The response must be written entirely in {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.language}}. Ensure the tone, grammar, and phrasing are natural and appropriate for that language.\n\nReturn the response as an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format: {\"summary\": \"&lt;insert the summary here>\"} and without enclosing it in any backticks, code blocks, or markdown formatting."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"summary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
      "variables": [],
      "errorHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "EMAIL",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "name": "toList",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "name": "ccList",
